{"availability":"available","full":"oduwsdl/ipwb","name":"ipwb","description":"InterPlanetary Wayback: A distributed and persistent archive replay system using IPFS","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":657,"forks":41,"created":"2016-03-04T15:01:33Z","updated":"2026-07-24T13:33:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["docker","ipfs","memento","memento-rfc","python","service-worker","warc","wayback","web-archiving"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.310Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.310Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.310Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:37:40.140Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:29.705Z","stars":657,"forks":41},{"at":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.310Z","stars":657,"forks":41}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["InterPlanetary Wayback (ipwb) facilitates permanence and collaboration in web archives by disseminating the contents of WARC files into the IPFS network. IPFS is a peer-to-peer content-addressable file system that inherently allows deduplication and facilitates opt-in replication. ipwb splits the header and payload of WARC response records before disseminating into IPFS to leverage the deduplication, builds a CDXJ index with references to the IPFS hashes that are returned, and combines the header and payload from IPFS at the time of replay.","InterPlanetary Wayback primarily consists of two scripts:","A pictorial representation of the ipwb indexing and replay process:"],"features":["ipwb/indexer.py - archival indexing script that takes the path to a WARC input, extracts the HTTP headers, HTTP payload (response body), and relevant parts of the WARC-response record header from the WARC specified and…","ipwb/replay.py - rudimentary replay script to resolve requests for archival content contained in IPFS for replay in the browser."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/oduwsdl/ipwb/blob/master/README.md","fin